{"uid":"include/wl_guard.h::wl_guard","name":"wl_guard","qualname":"wl_guard","kind":"type_alias","file":"include/wl_guard.h","line":21,"end_line":21,"language":"h","signature":"typedef struct wl_guard wl_guard;","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"wl_guard -- keeps the Wayland connection drained while the GUI thread is busy.","description":"A compositor queues events for a client in a small buffer (4 KiB) backed by the socket; a\nclient that does not read for a few seconds while the pointer moves gets DISCONNECTED\n(\"libwayland: Data too big for buffer ... error in client communication\"). Freedom blocks its\nGUI thread on page loads, image fetches and big layouts, so a helper thread reads the socket\nmeanwhile. It uses libwayland's documented multi-thread pattern: wl_display_prepare_read_queue\non a PRIVATE (always empty) queue, so the events are only enqueued -- every handler still runs\non the GUI thread, in order, when the main loop dispatches. See spec/wl_guard.md.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"include/wl_guard.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
